<p>The European Commission opened a formal investigation into Snapchat and said it had preliminarily found that Pornhub, Stripchat, XNXX and XVideos failed to keep minors away from adult content, stepping up the EU&#x27;s push to enforce child-safety rules under the Digital Services Act. Brussels said the cases focus on whether the platforms have effective age checks and other protections against risks such as grooming, sexual exploitation and exposure to harmful material. EU tech chief Henna Virkkunen said children are reaching adult content at younger ages and that platforms must use &quot;robust, privacy-preserving and effective&quot; safeguards. The Commission also pointed to a broader effort to strengthen online protections for minors across the bloc. The scrutiny could lead to fines under the DSA, while the EU is preparing an age-verification app for launch in 2027 as part of a more standardized approach to keeping underage users safer online.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/hD8rJQVplm7R44sgDFYDmTgGBieTdO2yhWq3EoqRU4G1pq7_Xohd2Z89_j152Cw5Gfns8yLhrIDD4HpSy5S16HjZHtZHxFJWezUg-TiW3sSeYdRJ8E-Nz78__E-0EzqSCwXQ_GsIoklvo8q5YAhCGXB1lGoVdEfJ6AwGB5tsaIyz6D-6lf5alo-mMXpLv7envzd1_zFgHm4y-eaNEfHQPrtDD41EbzQtE1FIb2kVuvvlIktLDSgneEoR' alt='European Commission-related image used with reporting on EU action against major online platforms over child-safety concerns.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Possible penalties: If Snapchat is found to have breached EU digital rules, its parent company, Snap, could face a fine of up to 6% of annual global turnover under the Digital Services Act.</li><li>Broader harm: The Commission said the four pornographic sites&#x27; failures do more than expose minors to explicit material; they can also harm young people&#x27;s mental health and reinforce negative gender attitudes.</li><li>Wider scrutiny: Politico reported that similar EU child-safety investigations have already targeted AliExpress, Facebook, Instagram and TikTok, showing the Commission is applying the rules across several major platforms.</li><li>Court backdrop: A California trial this week found Meta and YouTube negligent for designing addictive platforms that harmed a child and ordered $3 million in damages, adding to wider pressure on tech companies over youth safety.</li></ul><blockquote>Children are accessing adult content at increasingly younger ages, and these platforms must put in place robust, privacy-preserving and effective measures to keep minors off their services, - Henna Virkkunen</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>European Commission: The Commission is treating these as child-protection cases under the DSA, saying Snapchat may expose children to grooming and sexual exploitation, while the adult sites may have failed to protect children&#x27;s rights and well-being. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/mar/26/brussels-opens-investigation-into-snapchat-amid-concern-over-childrens-safety'>The Guardian</a>, <a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/26/eu-accuses-four-porn-sites-of-allowing-children-access-adult-content_6751841_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Snapchat: A company spokesperson said user safety and well-being are a top priority and that Snapchat was built with privacy and safety protections, including additional safeguards for teenagers. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/protection-des-mineurs-snapchat-visee-par-une-enquete-de-la-commission-europeenne/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>EU member states: Politico reported that EU countries have made child protection a top priority and are pushing the Commission to do more, reflecting growing political demand for stronger enforcement. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/protection-des-mineurs-snapchat-visee-par-une-enquete-de-la-commission-europeenne/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/online-porn-sites-putting-kids-safety-at-risk-eu-says/a-76547658'>Online porn sites putting kids&#x27; safety at risk, EU says</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/mar/26/brussels-opens-investigation-into-snapchat-amid-concern-over-childrens-safety'>Brussels opens investigation into Snapchat amid concern over children’s safety</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/26/eu-accuses-four-porn-sites-of-allowing-children-access-adult-content_6751841_4.html'>EU accuses four porn sites of allowing children access adult content</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/protection-des-mineurs-snapchat-visee-par-une-enquete-de-la-commission-europeenne/'>Protection des mineurs : Snapchat visée par une enquête de la Commission européenne</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/technology/pornhub-stripchat-xnxx-xvideos-charged-with-breaching-eu-tech-rules-risk-fines/article70791020.ece'>Pornhub, Stripchat, XNXX, XVideos charged with breaching EU tech rules, risk fines</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>